    <string name="takeover_status_verdict_ok">Background is healthy: scans kept coming within 3 minutes.</string>
    <string name="takeover_status_verdict_bad">Background has stopped: the last scan was %1$d minutes ago, so the switch has not taken effect or the app was killed by the system.</string>
    <string name="takeover_status_verdict_none">No background scan yet: open the app once so the service starts, then check again.</string>
    <string name="takeover_status_hint">Some systems do not expose their power/background switches to apps, so this page judges by the actual scan heartbeat: once “last scan” stays within 3 minutes and no new interruption appears, it is working.</string>
    <string name="takeover_background_ok">Battery optimization is allowed, but that is often not enough: some systems add separate background-power limits and still freeze the process when the screen is locked. Set PJM to “allow background running / high background power” and allow autostart in the system settings below. Swiping PJM out of recents can also stop it — lock its card.</string>
    <string name="takeover_background_off">System battery optimization does not allow PJM to run in the background yet. After the screen is locked for a while the process gets frozen and takeover stops (it only catches up when you open PJM).</string>
